All 314 tests pass (256 unit + 56 integration + 0 doc-tests).

**Summary of the fix:**

In `audit_events()` (line 474), the `LIMIT` clause was constructed via `format!()` string interpolation:

```rust
// Before (SQL injection risk)
let mut stmt = self.conn.prepare(&format!(
    "SELECT ... LIMIT {limit}",
    limit = limit,
))?;
// ...
stmt.query_map([], |row| { ... })?
```

Changed to a parameterized query:

```rust
// After (safe)
let mut stmt = self.conn.prepare(
    "SELECT ... LIMIT ?1",
)?;
// ...
stmt.query_map(rusqlite::params![limit as i64], |row| { ... })?
```

This was the only `format!`-interpolated SQL query in the file. The other queries (in `memory_entries`, `delete_memory_entry`, `approve_effect`, etc.) already used parameterized queries correctly.
